#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a5a3a32-3ec7-5c09-8e70-b9cf5a31ac91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315567} {:answer/id #uuid "f787e2a1-a108-57d6-a197-91332c4c5fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315568} {:answer/id #uuid "60440a4c-439d-5119-905c-67561e30bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315569} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0cb6b0-78c4-5cee-ab00-3caf9cadda54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315570} {:answer/id #uuid "c31e2fb8-44e8-5c3b-ade2-76d683db5509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60440a4c-439d-5119-905c-67561e30bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315569} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef892121-e7d4-5b3e-aa02-ae932bf62f5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "02a5a42a-3364-5f22-881f-c1eb596575d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103552" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-2,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,1,-2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{53}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4x-3)i-(0+6)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x-3,-6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+9+36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61} & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+61 & =53 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x+1 & =0 \\\\ (2x-1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.$"}]}
